<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Trino ODBC Driver</title><style>
<!--@STYLE@-->
</style></head>
<body>
<div class="head">
  <img src="@LOGO_DATA_URI@" alt="Trino logo">
  <div><h1>Trino ODBC Driver @VERSION@ is installed</h1><p class="sub">@DRIVER_MANAGER_LABEL@ &middot; macOS @ARCH@</p></div>
</div>

<h2>Installed files</h2>
<ul>
  <li><code>@INSTALL_DIR@/lib/libtrinoodbc.dylib</code> &mdash; the driver (and the libraries it needs)</li>
  <li><code>@INSTALL_DIR@/share/odbc.ini.example</code> &mdash; a DSN for every authentication type</li>
  <li><code>@INSTALL_DIR@/docs/</code> &mdash; the documentation (<code>INSTALL-MACOS.md</code>, <code>CONNECTION-OPTIONS.md</code>)</li>
</ul>
<p>The driver is registered as <b>Trino ODBC Driver</b> @REGISTRATION@.</p>

<h2>Register a data source (DSN)</h2>
<p>Add a section to @DSN_FILES@:</p>
<pre>[ODBC Data Sources]
TrinoProd=Trino ODBC Driver

[TrinoProd]
Driver=Trino ODBC Driver
Host=your-trino-host
Port=8443
AuthenticationType=LDAP
UID=your-user
SSL=1
Catalog=hive
Schema=default
; default Europe/Istanbul (UTC+03:00); another IANA zone or "system"
;TimeZone=system</pre>
<p>Then test it with <code>@TEST_COMMAND@</code>.</p>

<p class="fine">The Trino logo is a trademark of the Trino Software Foundation, shown only to
indicate compatibility; no endorsement is implied.</p>
</body>
</html>
